\f1\fs22 Agent Jones traced the ambulance and fumed with brick-walled impatience when he discovered the orderlies gave fake names: Dick van Dyke and Rick von Reich. Why would they bother? There\'92s nothing beyond the reach of PAPER. Jones turned up their true identities in seconds.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick and Rick were part-time PAPER contractors, according to their records and remuneration history. They were just grunts. Punks. The meat wagon was a side-gig for them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Paranoia boiled Jones\'92 thoughts\'97the company must be running a side-operation on him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Guns are a first resort. Agent Jones corralled Rick and Dick at muzzle-point and hauled them to a stony, truncated-pyramid of a building known only as Truth Central. Inside, a receptionist allocated him the required suite, where Truth clinicians dressed Dick and Rick for interrogation in experience sheaths\'97tight, translucent head-to-toe suits.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Experience sheaths were originally invented by the Playful Therapeutics Consortium, a group of visionaries who believed modern civilisation\'92s most urgent problem was \'93insufficient novelty in full-body masturbation.\'94 Their aspirations lasted until the first product recall (apparently masturbation 
\f2\i could
\f1\i0  now send you blind, and peel your skin off), after which the government quietly acquired the patent.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>To the untrained eye, an experience sheath looks like a latex wetsuit designed by a committee of sadists, physiotherapists, and divorce lawyers: head-to-toe, disturbingly translucent, and contoured in all the wrong places. Early versions were prone to static, over-compression, or folding small appendages irreversibly inward. The latest Truth-brand sheaths are soft, hypoallergenic, and only occasionally cause phantom no-limb syndrome in casual users.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The true technological marvel is not the suit, but the Console: a festival of sliders, rotary dials, pictograms, blinking emergency lights, and at least one enormous purple button labelled 
\fs20 ARE YOU SURE?
\fs22  into which Sheaths are directly plugged. Each moment, the operator cues up micro-adjustments to simulate everything from a warm foot spa to your foot being lovingly removed with garden shears, routed straight into the suffering nerve endings of the lucky wearer.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It\'92s shockingly precise: a skilled clinician can dial in mild tingles, a sunburn, the distinct sensation of a leech working up your sinuses, or the moment you realise your lover has mistakenly sent erotic videos to your grandmother. And should the operator lack sufficient imagination, the Console comes pre-loaded with over 3,000 government-certified \'93narrative overlays,\'94 including \'93Mock Amputation\'94, \'93Burning Cock\'94 (very popular in the halls of People and Culture), \'93I Never Knew Weevils Could Get in There\'94, and \'93Feel of Dropped Pie, Just as You Were About to Eat It.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Actual injury is so twentieth-century. The genius of the sheath is in fooling everything above the collarbone. Terror, confusion, and shame ramp up the realism until the subject could swear, legally and under oath, that their left toe is in a bucket of piranhas. This effect is so potent that government studies recommend debriefing with at least two litres of hot cocoa and a fun-size therapy animal.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And the ultimate punchline? Not only can genuine trauma be dished out on demand, but it can be copied, looped, remixed, and \'93bespoke curated\'94 for repeat effect. A single needle prick or digit-lopping is saved to memory, then replayed at a tap, while the subject begs for their lawyer, therapist, or mother, until the confession comes. Interrogators now boast of streaming their greatest hits from a convenient drop-down menu. Clean, scalable, and ideal for any modern bureaucracy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Experience sheaths: for when you absolutely, positively need to deliver the precise emotional resonance of a medieval rack, without the inconvenient paperwork, bloodstains, or union complaints. Available in four sizes, plus travel mini.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Rick and Dick panicked, as they always did, and clawed at the thin yet durable film covering their faces until clinicians restrained them in scratchy plastic-carbon-fibre chairs. Jones had demanded those for the occasion. Normally, they\'92d strap Truth candidates into medical couches designed for extended use, but Jones preferred these, his favourite interrogation chairs. Blood and tissue hosed right off, facilitating a speedy turnover of informants during busy times. Jones missed the old ways of belting the crap out of a target, hoping confession would come none too soon. Sometimes he would continue anyway. For special occasions, he still carried a chef\'92s roll filled with gleaming stainless steel knives, saws, drills, and other devices with cutting wheels and pointy bits.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones stood behind the clinician at the console while two more connected wires to the sheaths. The console clinician started the baseline diagnostics and watched a pair of flat screens while Rick and Dick giggled and \'93ouched\'94 as the sheaths delivered ever more fine-tuned stimuli. Eventually Rick and Dick began moaning, their sheaths stretching and accommodating their tumescence.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician flicked a switch. \'93They\'92re ready for experience,\'94 she told Agent Jones.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You will cut off the pinkies.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What?\'94 The clinician clamped her jaw shut and gave Agent Jones large, defiant eyes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Cut off the pinkies.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But they\'92re compliant,\'94 the clinician objected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones glared and tightened the knot of his red tie.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician swallowed. \'93Cutting off subjects\'92 fourth fingers,\'94 she confirmed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Rick and Dick howled in gasping terror.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones snarled. Though experience induction was more effective than physical injury, it could, for example, precisely replicate previous trauma. He wished there could be blood. His easy-clean chairs demanded it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Please!\'94 Dick said. \'93We said we\'92d cooperate. Just tell us what you want us to say.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Tell me about Emil Kalheri,\'94 Agent Jones said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Who?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Cut off the thumbs.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Special Agent\'85\'94 the clinician began.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Cut off the thumbs.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician shrank in her seat, and administered the experience.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick and Rick keened and bucked against their restraints. Rick\'92s chair tipped over. Clinicians went to right it; Agent Jones waved them away. He looked upon the informants with disgust. \'93Cut the stimuli.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Relieved, the clinician complied. Rick and Dick whimpered in the afterglow of their pain.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones said to them, \'93I ask about your delivery to Sunny Contemplations Funeral Home.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We make many\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sure,\'94 Dick interrupted Rick. \'93Whatever you want.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Jones peeled back the face flap of the suit from both interrogation subjects. \'93This suit.\'94 Agent Jones pulled Emil\'92s suit coat from a bag and held it up like washing on a line.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes! Yes!\'94 Rick said, with hope he might escape this after all. \'93I remember the suit.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The guy was just lying there, dead in the street,\'94 Dick added.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones contemplated, which was always hard work. \'93You stole from the body.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No! We\'92d never rob the dead.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Administer Burning Cock,\'94 Agent Jones instructed the clinician.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician recoiled, her hands jerked away from the console.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No! Please! We\'92re telling the truth!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But I think I know who could have,\'94 Rick offered. \'93That\'92s good, right? No need for roast cock-a-doodle?\'94 He giggled like a maniac.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Go on,\'94 Agent Jones said, with some disappointment.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There was this guy, you know? A cleaner.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A cleaner? Agent Jones ground his teeth and exhaled. There was a cleaner at Travis Teh\'92s office. And a cleaner at the scene of Emil Kalheri\'92s death? The cleaner must be an enemy operative.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We didn\'92t see him at first,\'94 Dick rambled. \'93He was hiding behind a cleaning cart, kneeling over the body.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Now I think about it, he was probably rummaging through the dead man\'92s clothes.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You apprehended this cleaner?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ah, no,\'94 Rick said, trembling. \'93We just told him to tax off. That\'92s it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Acquiring a taste for Agent Jones\'92 brutality in the face of Rick and Dick\'92s obvious incompetence, the console clinician squared her shoulders and took to her controls. \'93Administering Burning Cock,\'94 she confirmed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>During the extended seconds of agony, screaming, thrashing, and fouling of sheaths, Agent Jones watched as if from the comfort of a private box at the opera. \'93Cut the stimuli,\'94 he said, once boredom loomed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It took Rick and Dick some time to regain their breath and regulate their sobbing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Describe the cleaner,\'94 Agent Jones said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Eurasian male, early thirties, one-point-seven tall, dark hair. Dressed in busted-arse overalls.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Describe the overalls.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Just normal overalls, dirty white, stuff in pockets, logo over the breast pocket.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What logo?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I can\'92t remember. Something Cleaning? Maybe,\'94 Rick offered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Something about magic?\'94 Dick riffed. \'93Magic Cleaning services?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones charged and threw over Dick\'92s chair so he was lying alongside Rick. \'93Let me assist your memory.\'94 He took a large needle, as thick as a pencil, from his pocket, and inserted it into the webbing of Dick\'92s fingers. Dick bucked, but Agent Jones held his hand firm while he twiddled the needle among sinews and blood vessels.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick screamed with primeval pain and anger.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Do you remember now?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick jerked and convulsed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How about now, tax-face? Huh? Put my contract on the line, will you?\'94 He stood and kicked Dick in the head. He turned on Rick.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Please,\'94 Rick cried. \'93Let me think! Please, just let me think! Something about magic\'85 luck\'85 no\'85  oh, tax, please help me\'85 chanting\'85 Chant Cleaning? No, no. Enchanted Cleaning. That\'92s it: Enchanted Cleaning Services.\'94
